WEBVTT

00:00.830 --> 00:05.310
<i>I've already gotten used to how narrow the sky 
looks when I look up in the business district.</i>

00:05.610 --> 00:07.050
<i>Every year, by the time I realize it,</i>

00:07.050 --> 00:09.570
<i>summer ends with me only 
having seen this sky.</i>

00:09.570 --> 00:13.100
<i>I'm sure the same thing 
will happen this year, too.</i>

00:13.720 --> 00:17.420
<i>All I do is waste summer while the 
rest of the world is having fun.</i>

00:17.410 --> 00:17.620
Shiki Souta

00:20.360 --> 00:21.850
Senpai?

00:22.680 --> 00:23.680
Hello?

00:23.680 --> 00:24.840
Good morning.

00:25.350 --> 00:26.920
Is something wrong?

00:26.920 --> 00:29.400
It's so early, and we're off today.

00:29.400 --> 00:31.040
What are you talking about?

00:31.340 --> 00:32.700
It's our beach day.

00:33.460 --> 00:34.220
What?

02:05.470 --> 02:09.980
<b>#23 
Summer Sky and Sea</b>

02:06.800 --> 02:11.320
Wow, this is my first time riding 
in a car with three rows of seats.

02:11.320 --> 02:13.890
I rented something we could all fit in.

02:14.760 --> 02:17.350
So, a final name check.

02:17.350 --> 02:18.690
You're Souma's friend...

02:18.690 --> 02:19.920
Hayate.

02:19.920 --> 02:21.670
Yes. Thank you for taking me.

02:21.670 --> 02:22.690
Shun, right?

02:22.690 --> 02:23.290
Right.

02:23.290 --> 02:25.720
And then, Igarashi-sensei.

02:26.410 --> 02:27.710
Sorry about this.

02:28.030 --> 02:30.250
And thank you so much.

02:28.210 --> 02:31.080
<b>Bow bow</b>

02:30.250 --> 02:31.690
Oh, my pleasure.

02:31.690 --> 02:34.550
Let's just forget all about 
work today and have some fun.

02:34.550 --> 02:35.730
That's a good idea.

02:35.730 --> 02:39.420
My brother, Motoharu-kun, and Mima-san 
have an interesting relationship, huh.

02:40.140 --> 02:43.110
I guess even Mima-san gets 
dates mixed up sometimes.

02:41.910 --> 02:43.120
Let's pick seats.

02:43.110 --> 02:45.640
Apparently he wrote it into 
his calendar one week off.

02:43.120 --> 02:45.100
I'm not going if I'm not in the back.

02:45.640 --> 02:47.360
That's Takayuki for you.

02:47.360 --> 02:50.090
Well, guys don't need much time 
to get ready for the beach.

02:50.090 --> 02:51.820
He'll get here fast.

02:52.190 --> 02:53.520
Speaking of which, Shun...

02:53.520 --> 02:54.050
Yeah?

02:54.060 --> 03:00.530
<b>Fully prepared</b>

02:54.060 --> 03:00.530
<b>Swim
trunks</b>

02:54.350 --> 02:56.500
Those are your swim trunks, right?

02:56.500 --> 02:58.380
As soon as we get there, 
I'm getting in the water.

02:58.380 --> 02:59.760
Is there a problem?

02:59.760 --> 03:00.520
No.

03:00.520 --> 03:02.730
Do those dry quickly, though?

03:02.730 --> 03:04.180
Huh? No idea.

03:04.180 --> 03:06.160
Did you bring something else to change into?

03:08.300 --> 03:09.530
Oh, he's here!

03:10.770 --> 03:12.200
I'm sorry. I'm late.

03:12.200 --> 03:14.420
I think this is the first 
time I've seen you running.

03:15.040 --> 03:17.370
Well, looks like everyone's here!

03:17.680 --> 03:19.460
Beach, here we come!

03:23.110 --> 03:24.060
Mima!

03:24.060 --> 03:24.540
Yes?

03:24.540 --> 03:27.410
I wanna have some beer once we arrive.

03:27.410 --> 03:28.500
Of course.

03:28.500 --> 03:30.140
I'll drive on the way back.

03:30.140 --> 03:31.090
Sweet!

03:31.090 --> 03:33.910
Just make sure you keep it to one beer.

03:33.910 --> 03:36.210
He's such a pain when he gets drunk.

03:36.210 --> 03:38.030
Come on, it's the beach!

03:38.030 --> 03:40.150
You and Shun are the only ones 
who are underage, right?

03:40.150 --> 03:40.620
Yup.

03:41.020 --> 03:43.010
What about you, Igarashi-sensei, Hayate?

03:43.010 --> 03:44.430
I can drink.

03:44.430 --> 03:45.780
Nice!

03:45.780 --> 03:48.750
I just turned twenty this 
spring, so I'm not really...

03:48.750 --> 03:51.890
Then I'll be your big brother 
and teach you how to drink.

03:51.890 --> 03:54.260
Are you really in a position to teach that?

03:55.440 --> 03:58.570
Hey, why don't we do 
beach-vocab-only shiritori?

03:58.570 --> 03:59.460
Let's start with K!

03:59.460 --> 04:02.080
K... K... Kelp.

04:02.080 --> 04:04.810
P?! P... P...

04:04.810 --> 04:06.730
Isn't beach vocab only too hard?

04:06.730 --> 04:08.000
P... P...

04:08.420 --> 04:10.380
I forgot the pump!

04:10.380 --> 04:12.210
And I even brought a swim ring.

04:12.210 --> 04:13.540
Ahh.

04:14.530 --> 04:16.610
Next, P from pump.

04:15.190 --> 04:16.610
<b>Using the time 
now to blow 
it up manually</b>

04:16.610 --> 04:18.510
We're still doing that?

04:18.510 --> 04:21.560
Okay. P... P... Pacific 
dotted butterflyfish.

04:21.560 --> 04:22.750
Say what?

04:22.750 --> 04:25.270
Um, I know I've seen something like that.

04:25.270 --> 04:26.690
Oh, true.

04:26.690 --> 04:28.660
I've seen this fish before.

04:28.660 --> 04:30.870
Do you know a lot about biology, Hayate?

04:30.870 --> 04:31.490
Not really.

04:31.740 --> 04:33.860
I used to look at picture 
encyclopedias a lot as a kid,

04:33.860 --> 04:35.850
so I randomly remembered it.

04:35.850 --> 04:37.780
<i>Now I feel like everyone thinks 
I was trying to show off.</i>

04:37.780 --> 04:38.830
<i>How embarrassing.</i>

04:38.830 --> 04:41.950
My teacher knows everything!

04:38.840 --> 04:41.880
<b>Triumphant</b>

04:41.950 --> 04:43.370
Please stop.

04:42.970 --> 04:44.050
<b>Salt in the wound</b>

04:44.440 --> 04:46.260
I want to see a dotted butterflyfish!

04:47.710 --> 04:50.730
<i>Before, my life never had a 
chance to be this lively,</i>

04:48.080 --> 04:50.710
It's like they just crossed a 
butterfly with a fish, huh?

04:51.090 --> 04:54.880
<i>but it all started on that day I forgot 
my wallet at the convenience store.</i>

04:53.390 --> 04:54.890
<b>Hakoniwa</b>

04:55.450 --> 04:58.190
<i>Now all of us are going 
to the beach together.</i>

04:55.900 --> 04:56.900
<b>Effectively a tutor</b>

04:55.900 --> 04:56.900
<b>Boom</b>

04:56.900 --> 04:57.770
<b>Meet</b>

04:59.340 --> 05:01.960
This is kind of great, huh?

05:03.300 --> 05:04.650
What did you say?

05:05.610 --> 05:06.900
Nothing.

05:07.230 --> 05:10.220
Hey, Shun, weren't you supposed 
to be blowing up the swim ring?

05:10.220 --> 05:11.000
Oh, yeah...

05:11.530 --> 05:13.300
The GPS says we're almost there.

05:14.780 --> 05:16.640
You can see the ocean from here!

05:19.810 --> 05:21.280
There it is!

05:22.350 --> 05:24.150
Don't forget this umbrella, okay?

05:24.150 --> 05:25.060
Okay.

05:25.380 --> 05:26.510
All right then, Mima.

05:26.510 --> 05:28.140
You're on guard duty first.

05:28.140 --> 05:28.650
Yes.

05:29.340 --> 05:31.020
All warmed up.

05:31.020 --> 05:31.940
Time to swim.

05:32.200 --> 05:34.730
I almost want to tell you to go 
to the pool with that get-up.

05:35.440 --> 05:36.790
Wanna race?

05:36.390 --> 05:38.120
Mima-san, I'll go ahead, then.

05:36.790 --> 05:39.750
I don't want to get my head wet.

05:38.120 --> 05:39.650
Yes, have fun.

05:40.050 --> 05:41.910
Don't go out too far!

05:42.200 --> 05:42.940
Okay!

05:42.940 --> 05:43.850
Sure.

05:44.760 --> 05:46.490
<i>The sky is so wide.</i>

05:46.970 --> 05:48.060
<i>So blue.</i>

05:58.660 --> 06:00.550
I'm knackered.

06:00.840 --> 06:03.260
Oh, sorry. Did I wake you up?

06:03.260 --> 06:04.560
Souma-kun.

06:04.560 --> 06:05.680
Are you taking a break?

06:05.680 --> 06:08.480
Yes. I couldn't keep up with Shun.

06:09.240 --> 06:11.130
I can take over watching our stuff.

06:11.130 --> 06:12.800
It's fine.

06:13.290 --> 06:15.420
Staying here is enough for me right now.

06:15.930 --> 06:17.110
It is?

06:19.530 --> 06:21.680
Do you mind if I talk to you?

06:21.680 --> 06:22.390
Go ahead.

06:22.890 --> 06:25.760
Which one of these do you think is better?

06:26.720 --> 06:30.290
These are the potential covers for that 
one girl making a CD of her own music.

06:32.040 --> 06:34.060
Is she the girl in the photo?

06:34.060 --> 06:34.670
Yes.

06:35.420 --> 06:36.940
Since it's her own music,

06:36.940 --> 06:40.880
I'd recommend the one where 
she's holding the guitar.

06:41.190 --> 06:42.710
That's what I thought too.

06:43.200 --> 06:46.130
This girl's voice is clear, like the sky,

06:46.130 --> 06:48.420
while the overall atmosphere of 
her music is all fluffy.

06:48.730 --> 06:51.660
So I prepared a version based 
on each of those two feelings.

06:52.310 --> 06:53.880
You made these?

06:53.880 --> 06:55.130
Yes.

06:55.130 --> 06:58.430
I figured I should take advantage of the 
summer break and try as many things as I can.

06:59.610 --> 07:02.140
It's impressive that you 
really actualized that idea.

07:02.140 --> 07:03.520
Oh, it's not much.

07:04.210 --> 07:07.140
At best, I'm only helping out a little bit.

07:07.140 --> 07:10.500
I can only do my stuff because 
others have already done the work.

07:10.780 --> 07:14.700
Seeing people like that makes me 
think I have to try my best too.

07:15.320 --> 07:17.560
Once you do try, your worldview expands,

07:17.560 --> 07:20.720
and it's neat to feel like 
your potential increased.

07:21.150 --> 07:22.660
I'm going to send it now.

07:24.630 --> 07:25.840
All right!

07:25.840 --> 07:28.040
I'm going to get some shaved ice.

07:28.040 --> 07:28.950
Wanna come with?

07:29.220 --> 07:32.410
No, I'll stay here and watch our things.

07:33.090 --> 07:34.140
See you later.

07:38.450 --> 07:41.820
<i>I feel like I was just told 
something important by someone</i>

07:41.820 --> 07:43.860
<i>fresh out the gates to chase their dreams.</i>

07:43.860 --> 07:46.260
<i>By a young person who's 
as passionate as the sun.</i>

07:46.830 --> 07:49.370
<i>I shouldn't get used to the narrow view 
of the sky in the business district.</i>

07:49.950 --> 07:51.000
Takayuki.

07:51.950 --> 07:53.630
I'll take over watching our stuff.

07:53.630 --> 07:56.030
We came all the way here, so why 
don't you go play in the waves?

07:56.480 --> 07:57.400
Well...

07:58.140 --> 08:00.450
<i>I feel inspired. The summer is so bright.</i>

08:01.710 --> 08:04.910
<i>This year's summer sky is so wide.</i>

08:05.350 --> 08:07.490
<i>Everyone else enjoys summer.</i>

08:07.490 --> 08:08.570
I'll go.

08:08.570 --> 08:09.630
Go have fun.

08:09.630 --> 08:12.350
<i>I'll see what it's all about.</i>

08:13.320 --> 08:14.370
What's wrong?

08:14.370 --> 08:15.980
I stepped on coral.

08:14.810 --> 08:16.960
<b></b>Ouch...

08:15.980 --> 08:16.960
Unlucky.

08:18.980 --> 08:20.630
<i>The line's pretty long.</i>

08:21.040 --> 08:23.410
<i>What kind of syrup should 
I get on my shaved ice?</i>

08:22.520 --> 08:23.730
<b></b>Peek

08:24.150 --> 08:26.320
Excuse me?

08:26.320 --> 08:26.950
Yes?

08:26.950 --> 08:29.720
Your shirt is inside out.

08:27.310 --> 08:28.520
<b>Whisper</b>

08:30.410 --> 08:31.300
<i>I said it.</i>

08:31.300 --> 08:32.610
<i>You finally got to say it!</i>

08:32.610 --> 08:34.070
Oh, you're right.

08:34.070 --> 08:35.320
I can see the tag.

08:35.320 --> 08:39.110
<i>And here we were almost dying 
from secondhand shame!</i>

08:40.060 --> 08:41.710
I didn't notice.

08:41.710 --> 08:43.160
Thank you.

08:43.160 --> 08:43.840
You know...

08:43.830 --> 08:44.830
<b>Throb</b>

08:44.080 --> 08:45.660
You know...

08:45.660 --> 08:47.790
<i>The fact that he seems unfazed is hot.</i>

08:48.030 --> 08:51.120
So, um, are you here with your friends?

08:51.120 --> 08:51.960
Yes.

08:51.960 --> 08:54.620
If you like, maybe later we could...

08:54.550 --> 08:55.180
<b>Step</b>

08:54.620 --> 08:55.520
Souma.

08:56.340 --> 08:57.760
<b>Tower</b>

08:57.080 --> 08:58.570
Who are these people?

08:58.570 --> 09:00.740
The people who let me know 
my shirt was inside out.

09:00.740 --> 09:02.220
Really? Embarrassing.

09:00.960 --> 09:03.300
<i>He looks like he came to hardcore swim!</i>

09:02.220 --> 09:03.300
Oh shut up.

09:03.300 --> 09:05.880
All right, bye, then!

09:05.880 --> 09:08.240
<i>Don't want to get in the 
way of the tryhards.</i>

09:08.240 --> 09:10.200
Yes, thank you.

09:11.150 --> 09:14.350
Shun, why are you wearing 
goggles even on land?

09:14.350 --> 09:15.610
They're like sunglasses.

09:15.850 --> 09:19.360
They'll probably leave much clearer 
tan lines than sunglasses.

09:20.790 --> 09:22.110
Damn, then I'll take them off.

09:22.110 --> 09:24.670
Cool, now it's easier to walk with you.

09:24.660 --> 09:32.130
<b>Ice</b>

09:24.670 --> 09:26.160
Are you buying something?

09:26.160 --> 09:27.300
I'm getting shaved ice.

09:27.300 --> 09:29.780
Half is enough for me, 
so you can eat the rest.

09:29.780 --> 09:31.070
You can pick the flavor.

09:31.070 --> 09:32.130
Then lemon.

09:33.380 --> 09:34.970
That looks so good!

09:35.290 --> 09:36.720
This is summer, right here.

09:36.720 --> 09:38.590
Will you hurry up and eat 
it before it all melts?

09:38.880 --> 09:41.770
You really take pictures of any old thing.

09:42.200 --> 09:43.180
That reminds me.

09:43.180 --> 09:45.390
Didn't you say you were making a CD cover?

09:45.390 --> 09:46.780
What happened with that?

09:46.780 --> 09:49.230
I just sent her some mock-ups.

09:49.680 --> 09:52.720
Usually she's really quick to respond, 
but she still hasn't said anything.

09:53.160 --> 09:54.440
She's probably thinking...

09:54.710 --> 09:56.650
about whether to approve them or not.

09:57.530 --> 09:58.990
It's so hot.

09:58.990 --> 10:00.840
Where's our umbrella again?

10:01.470 --> 10:02.500
<i>That makes sense.</i>

10:02.500 --> 10:04.320
<i>Even if I'm happy with it,</i>

10:04.320 --> 10:07.540
<i>it's pointless if the person
I made it for doesn't like it.</i>

10:09.130 --> 10:13.510
<i>Maybe she doesn't like it, and now she's 
struggling to come up with a polite response.</i>

10:14.290 --> 10:18.310
<i>What if she's thinking that it was 
a mistake to ask me to do it?</i>

10:59.970 --> 11:04.970
<b>Cool and Awkward Guys</b>

10:59.970 --> 11:04.980
<b>Coming up next</b>

11:04.980 --> 11:09.970
<b>We hope you'll tune in again!</b>

11:04.980 --> 11:09.970
<b>We hope you'll tune in again!</b>
